/figure>
<p id=3D"mwLg">In 1835, Lord King (as he then was) married as his first wif=
e <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ada_Lovelace=
" title=3D"Ada Lovelace" id=3D"mwLw">Ada Byron</a>, the only daughter of th=
e poet <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lord_By=
ron" title=3D"Lord Byron" id=3D"mwMA">Lord Byron</a> and his wife <a rel=3D=
"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anne_Isabella_Byron,_Ba=
roness_Byron" title=3D"Anne Isabella Byron, Baroness Byron" class=3D"mw-red=
irect" id=3D"mwMQ">Anne Isabella Milbanke</a>. He was created <b id=3D"mwMg=
">Viscount Ockham</b> and <b id=3D"mwMw">Earl of Lovelace</b> in 1838, and =
appointed <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lord=
_Lieutenant_of_Surrey" title=3D"Lord Lieutenant of Surrey" id=3D"mwNA">Lord=
 Lieutenant of Surrey</a> in 1840, a post he held until his death.<sup abou=
t=3D"#mwt19" class=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"cite_ref-Burke_3-0" rel=3D"dc=
:references" typeof=3D"mw:Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot=
;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Burke&quot;},&quot;bod=
y&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-Burke-3&quot;}}">=
<a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_King-Noel,_1st_Earl_of_Lov=
elace#cite_note-Burke-3" id=3D"mwNQ"><span class=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=3D"=
mwNg"><span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwNw">[</span>3<span class=3D"cite=
-bracket" id=3D"mwOA">]</span></span></a></sup> The Lovelace title was chos=
en to mark the fact that Ada was, through the families of Byron, Milbanke, =
Noel and Lovelace, a descendant of the extinct <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baron_Lovelace" title=3D"Baron Lovelace" =
id=3D"mwOQ">Barons Lovelace</a>. The couple had three children: <a rel=3D"m=
w:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byron_King-Noel,_Viscount=
_Ockham" title=3D"Byron King-Noel, Viscount Ockham" id=3D"mwOg">Byron</a> (=
born 1836), <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/An=
ne_Blunt,_15th_Baroness_Wentworth" title=3D"Anne Blunt, 15th Baroness Wentw=
orth" id=3D"mwOw">Anne</a> (born 1837), and <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"=
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ralph_King-Milbanke,_2nd_Earl_of_Lovelace" ti=
tle=3D"Ralph King-Milbanke, 2nd Earl of Lovelace" id=3D"mwPA">Ralph</a> (bo=
rn 1839). Lady Lovelace died in 1852, leaving her husband, in his forties, =
a widower. </p>

<p id=3D"mwPQ">In 1860, the Earl's eldest son, Byron, succeeded <a rel=3D"m=
w:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lady_Byron" title=3D"Lady=
 Byron" id=3D"mwPg">his maternal grandmother</a> to become 12th <a rel=3D"m=
w:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baron_Wentworth" title=3D=
"Baron Wentworth" id=3D"mwPw">Baron Wentworth</a> according to its special =
remainder. However, he died, still unmarried, just two years later, and his=
 brother <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ralph=
_King-Milbanke,_2nd_Earl_of_Lovelace" title=3D"Ralph King-Milbanke, 2nd Ear=
l of Lovelace" id=3D"mwQA">Ralph</a> became 13th Baron Wentworth. In 1861, =
Ralph assumed by Royal licence the surname of Milbanke in lieu of Noel.</p>

