<p id=3D"mwQg">Lord Lovelace was appointed <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"h=
ttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colonel_(United_Kingdom)#Colonel_of_the_Regime=
nt" title=3D"Colonel (United Kingdom)" id=3D"mwQw">Colonel</a> of the <a re=
l=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2nd_Royal_Surrey_Mi=
litia" title=3D"2nd Royal Surrey Militia" id=3D"mwRA">2nd Royal Surrey Mili=
tia</a> on 14 August 1852. He resigned this command on 11 April 1870, when =
he was appointed <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wi=
ki/Colonel_(United_Kingdom)#Honorary_Colonel" title=3D"Colonel (United King=
dom)" id=3D"mwRQ">Honorary Colonel</a> of the regiment (which became the <a=
 rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/3rd_(2nd_Royal_S=
urrey_Militia)_Battalion,_Queen's_(Royal_West_Surrey_Regiment)" title=3D"3r=
d (2nd Royal Surrey Militia) Battalion, Queen's (Royal West Surrey Regiment=
)" class=3D"mw-redirect" id=3D"mwRg">3rd Battalion, Queen's (Royal West Sur=
rey Regiment)</a>, a position he held until his death.<sup about=3D"#mwt20"=
 class=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"cite_ref-Burke_3-1" rel=3D"dc:references"=
 typeof=3D"mw:Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&=
